{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523655-is-there-something-that-makes-a-human-impossible-to-be-embraced","id":1523655,"title":"Is there something that makes a human impossible to be Embraced?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-10-05T13:15:48-07:00","id":1523655,"title":"Is there something that makes a human impossible to be Embraced?","content":"From the lore perspective, are there humans that can not be Embraced because of something innate in them? Like something that would make a, say, random Joe drop dead instead of being Embraced no matter what generation blood the to-be-sire possessed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28209-kaelharan","user":"Kaelharan","date":". 10-05-2023, 04:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28209-kaelharan","name":"Kaelharan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-06T01:21:27-07:00","id":1523685,"title":"","content":"As far as I know, there is no specific Merit or Flaw to that effect. Success of the Embrace was always something left for the ST to decide.<br /> <br /> There are some conditions that make an Embrace more likely to fail according to lore, however.<br /> <br /> - Imbued can not be monsters. HtR makes a big point of this and emphasizes that Hunters are still human. They are hardly Joe Average, though.<br /> - Kinfolk are mentioned to receive Gaia's mercy and will mostly just drop dead. I imagine Kinfolk of the breeds that just can not be turned get some extra help with that. It's not 100% though.<br /> - True Faith, if I recall correctly, makes an Embrace extremely unlikely to work.<br /> - Fate. Seriously, it's a mechanic. A mortal could simply be fated to die instead of turning.<br /> <br /> There are several more scenarios that require the intervention of another supernatural, like Necromancy rituals or certain powers. While that's not exactly innate to the mortal, having a Wraith of a deceased loved one follow you around who rips out your soul just before the Embrace is something that can narratively happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-06T02:38:21-07:00","id":1523689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523655-is-there-something-that-makes-a-human-impossible-to-be-embraced?p=1523685#post1523685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Fate. Seriously, it's a mechanic. A mortal could simply be fated to die instead of turning.</div> </div> </div> </div>A very interesting detail. Where can I read some more about this mechanic? Or is it a thing for a gm to decide?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28209-kaelharan","user":"Kaelharan","date":". 10-06-2023, 05:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28209-kaelharan","name":"Kaelharan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-06T10:18:53-07:00","id":1523723,"title":"","content":"It's certainly something to talk through with the ST. The relevant Merits/Flaws would be Dark Fate (-5) in the V20 Core and Destiny (+4) in various splats, but for Vampire it's in the old Player Guides. Aside from those, fate is a much more tangible concept in the WOD and there are several powers that directly manipulate it. Prophecies, oracles, divination, and so on are things that actually work. There's a whole school of Magick dealing with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-08T11:04:29-07:00","id":1523826,"title":"","content":"I think theirs a merit for it. The only other exceptions are if the body is too damaged upon embrace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-08T12:11:45-07:00","id":1523827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kaelharan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523655-is-there-something-that-makes-a-human-impossible-to-be-embraced#post1523655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the lore perspective, are there humans that can not be Embraced because of something innate in them?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a Warrior Valeren 4th level power called <b>Ending the Watch</b><br /> The Salubri using that power grants a quiet, painless death to a willing subject.<br /> <b>System:</b> To End the Watch, the vampire places her hand on the subject's chest. The player spends a Willpower point. The subject must be willing to end her life. If she struggles or refuses, the attempt fails. her heart slowly ceases to beat, and the subject appears to go into a deep, peaceful sleep. Curiously, and individual affected by this power may not be subsequently Embraced, nor will she become a wraith.<br /> <br /> It is a very.... complicated and sensitive topic<br /> Now one can argue, if some one truly wishes to die that desire is so strong - with the help of the power - literally prevent anything, Embrace, Nacromancy to call back, anything, including God Almighty's Seventh House to defy that Will<br /> This could be - from a Mage persepctive- reality shaping power of the Sleepers, the will to die so strong it literally bends reality and prevent anything to happen<br /> <br /> With Bardo's 6th level of power called the<b> Boon of Anubis</b> a vampire can protect a mortal from Embrace, leaving instructions for Anubis, the judge of the dead, not to take this particular mortal to his scales. If the mortal is Embraced while under the power of this Discipline, she simply sleeps for a full night and day, and awakens aching and sick, but unharmed.<br /> <br /> If you're using lore from the other lines, kinfolk have a (very) small chance of manifesting gnosis (they need a merit for that), which among its benefits can prevent the embrace from happening (on V20 rules they'd get a roll of Gnosis, difficulty 6, success results in peaceful death, failure results in pur epain that lasts until sunrise, when they finaly die, and a botch results in being Embrace).<br /> <br /> (I know these things are not &quot;innate&quot; just wanted to show, there are ways to encounter a failed Embrace - and from the Vampire point of view who don't know whats behind it coudl seem innate)<br /> <br /> \u200bIf I remember right, there was a Ravnos (?) (or Malkavian?) fiction in the Revised core book where a Kindred worried he'd given the blood a little too late and just kept waiting for his lover to rise. Just waiting. Waiting...<br /> So the Embrace tho' not stated rarely if ever works on some one who is dead more than a few minutes<br /> Or if the vitae was out from the vampire's body for too long - and not preserved some supernatural ways - usually it has to be done immediately.<br /> And of course there is the possibility.... well, the vampie simply had no idea how to Embrace. I mean it is not something many could recall or the Sire included in the &quot;What you must know&quot; lessons. Actually many Sire I think proposefully not tell this their Child (or outright lies to them how to do it) to avoid any potential Tradition breach - if the Fledgeling don't know how to Embrace, the chance she in panic after her first kill tries to &quot;save&quot; the victim and commit a &quot;crime&quot; lessen greatly - and following what you could read in books and see TV? Good luck with those.<br /> <br /> But as others said, usually Fate is in work - if an avarage Joe's fate is not to be a Vampire? He will not turns in to one<br /> The Lore is full of failed Embraces - starting with Cappadocius's Embrace (tho' he is not failed, but the Wraiths he pissed off managed to hold back enough of his soul so when he was Embraced. Part of Cappadocius never returned from the underworld. Much of his knowledge and self-awareness were lost in that faulty Embrace, and the being who returned was not quite he who began the journey. Cappadocius' very soul had been fragmented, and that is why he harbored such a fascination for the dead: Even when he himself did not realize it, he was constantly seeking the missing portions of himself.)\u200b<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}